  "title": "Actual balanced finite-count normalized sum law converges to Gaussian",
  "mode": "faithfulPaper",
  "source_anchor": "arXiv:2609.06906v1 S4.E6 omitted Gaussian LSI background; pinned Mathlib db584cd6 CentralLimitTheorem.tendsto_charFun_inv_sqrt_mul_pow / LevyConvergence; authored Bool-count law adapter",
  "target_statement": "theorem balanced_count_sum_tendsto_gaussian :\n    ∃ laws : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure ℝ,\n      (∀ n : ℕ, (laws n : Measure ℝ) =\n        (((Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ •\n          (Measure.count : Measure (Fin n → Bool))).map\n          (fun ε : Fin n → Bool => (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ *\n            ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1))) ∧\n      (laws 0 : Measure ℝ) = Measure.dirac 0 ∧\n      Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => laws (n + 1)) atTop\n        (𝓝 (⟨gaussianReal 0 1, inferInstance⟩ : ProbabilityMeasure ℝ))\n",
